      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Another account of the descent of the Ganges, however, states",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "that Jahnu was a Rishi performing penance and that the Gan-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "ges in its course having disturbed the sage in his concentration",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "by flooding the country where he was, the sage in anger stopp-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "ed the course of the river by pressing it under his thigh. At",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "Bhàgiratha’s earnest entreaties, however, he let the stream flow",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "again. कन्दर and दरी are usually given as synonymous terms;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "( दरी तु कन्दरो वा स्त्री Amara; while कुञ्ज has a different shade of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "meaning. निकुञ्जकुञ्जौ वा क्लीबे लतादिपिहितोदरे Amara. A कुञ्ज is a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "hollow in a mountain covered over with creepers and other",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "plants. दरी is a cave, a hollow dug out or opened up in the side",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "of a hill; and कन्दर, though synonymous with दरी should rather",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "be taken here to mean the gorge or defile between two hills, in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "which sense it is used in sl. 26. क्वचित्—somewhere. For दरी read",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "तटी in the text.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 80. रम्यं साधु &c.—company of religious people can not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "but be pleasing. तरलम्—glistening, beaming; cf. न प्रभातरलं ज्योति-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "रुदेति वसुधातलात् S'ak. Rámarshi gives चपलम् as its explanation.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "उपाहित—placed ( there, by anger. ). अनित्यतामुपगते &c.—When",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "the mind has become unsteady, i. e. is not in its usual mood,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "nothing pleases it. Or when the thoughts of the mutability of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "this existence cross the mind, it becomes distracted and then",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "it cannot relish anything earthly, except the joy of Brahman.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 81. प्रीतये—the dat. case as indicating the result. दीपांकुर-",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the tapering flame. छाया—shadow. Râmarshi explains it by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "आतपप्रत्यनीका—( the contrary of light ) which Mr. Telang does",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "not accept. He gives it the meaning of ‘flame’; but as the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "word दीपांकुर already occurs the word छाया would be redundant",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "if it were taken to signify ‘flame.’ The shadow thrown by the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "flickering flame of a lamp is even more unsteady than the flame",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "on account of its magnitude. आकलय्य—having fully compre-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "hended or known.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 82. आसंसारं-त्रिभुवनम् &c.—( Searching through ) the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "three worlds where the course of worldly life prevails:—Telang,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "The mind is deeply attached to sensual objects as the elephant",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
